  "body": {
    "id": "thm:finite-design-regret",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "Uniformly for \\(p\\in\\mathcal P\\), the certified offset satisfies \\(J_N(p,\\gamma_\\epsilon)-\\inf_{|\\gamma|\\le G}J_N(p,\\gamma)\\le\\epsilon+o(1)\\).",
    "free_symbols": [
      "JN",
      "p",
      "gamma",
      "gammaepsilon",
      "G",
      "epsilon",
      "Pbox"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "ass:rate-bounds",
      "ass:rate-membership",
      "ass:staffing-window",
      "ass:staffing-cost-positive",
      "ass:information-cost-positive",
      "def:design-objective",
      "def:certificate-algorithm",
      "thm:diffusion-poisson",
      "thm:certified-capacity-design"
    ],
    "justification": "A diffusion optimizer is operationally meaningful only if its certificate transfers to the actual integer-capacity experiment.",
    "gap": "Borst, Mandelbaum, and Reiman prove recovery for an open-queue cost, not the finite-source inferential objective here.",
    "consumer": "The staffing manager can implement \\(M_N=\\lceil Na+\\gamma_\\epsilon\\sqrt N\\rceil\\) with asymptotically certified finite-system regret.",
    "proof_tex": "By the uniform energy convergence in the diffusion theorem and the common\npositive lower bound on \\(V_{0,N}+V_{1,N}\\) and \\(V_0+V_\\gamma\\), the\ninequality\n\\[\n |\\sqrt x-\\sqrt y|\\leq\\frac{|x-y|}{\\sqrt x+\\sqrt y}\n\\]\nimplies\n\\[\n \\Delta_N:=\\sup_{p\\in\\mathcal P,\\,|\\gamma|\\leq G}\n |J_N(p,\\gamma)-J(p,\\gamma)|\\longrightarrow0.                    \\tag{56}\n\\]\nThe capacity certificate gives\n\\(J(p,\\gamma_\\epsilon)-\\inf_{|\\gamma|\\leq G}J(p,\\gamma)\\leq\\epsilon\\).\nAdding and subtracting \\(J\\) and applying (56) yields, uniformly in \\(p\\),\n\\[\n\\begin{split}\n J_N(p,\\gamma_\\epsilon)-\\inf_{|\\gamma|\\leq G}J_N(p,\\gamma)\n &\\leq J(p,\\gamma_\\epsilon)-\\inf_{|\\gamma|\\leq G}J(p,\\gamma)\n      +2\\Delta_N\\\\\n &\\leq\\epsilon+o(1),\n\\end{split}\n\\]\nwhich is the claimed finite-system regret certificate.",
